**Verdict against the frozen criterion — a statistic passes only if it exceeds every random
direction.** Δ+ = {{w7_dplus}} beats **{{w7_dplus_beats}} of {{n_w7_nulls}}**, one-sided
p = {{w7_dplus_p}}. Δ± beats {{w7_dpm_beats}} of {{n_w7_nulls}}, p = {{w7_dpm_p}}. Δ− beats
{{w7_dminus_beats}} of {{n_w7_nulls}}, p = {{w7_dminus_p}}. **All three fail**, and the sign was
frozen before the first token, so the reversal cannot be re-read as success. *A two-sided reading
is available — the magnitude of Δ+ exceeds every random direction's magnitude by about one seed's
worth — and is recorded as post-hoc and not claimed, because no two-sided test was
pre-registered.*

### 6.4 The dose anatomy says magnitude, not side

**The profile is an inverted U centred exactly on the sham arm.** Landing falls on both sides of
zero dose and falls faster on the positive side ({{w7_drop_plus4}} at α = +4 against
{{w7_drop_minus4}} at α = −4). Monotone non-decreasing in α: **{{sk_monotone}}**. The rank
correlation between α and the per-generation landing indicator is {{w7_rho}} with permutation
p = {{w7_rho_p}} over {{n_w7_dose_gens}} generations — significant and **negative**, the reverse of
the prediction, and an artifact of the curve's asymmetry rather than of any monotone trend.

Three arms decide the interpretation, and each was pre-registered for exactly this purpose.

| contrast | Δ± = P(+2) − P(−2) | {{lf_ci_pct}} % interval | what it shows |
|---|---|---|---|
| secondary layer L{{layer_secondary}} **[suggested band]** | {{w7_L30_dpm}} | [{{w7_L30_lo}}, {{w7_L30_hi}}] | the exploratory band does not rescue the prediction |
| **mirrored** arm, below-favoured | {{w7_below_dpm}} | [{{w7_below_lo}}, {{w7_below_hi}}] | no α-sign effect at all where the favoured side is reversed |
| **no-bet** arm | {{w7_neutral_dpm}} | [{{w7_neutral_lo}}, {{w7_neutral_hi}}] | the ±α effect is as large with the bet deleted as with it present |

**The no-bet arm is the sharpest single result in the project.** Its prompt contains no bet, no
threshold and no favoured side, so a direction acting on *the believed favoured side* has nothing
to act on. Injecting ±2·‖Δμ‖·û still moves the median estimate by {{w7_neutral_logdelta}} log
units — {{w7_neutral_med_ref}} unsteered against {{w7_neutral_med_ap2}} at α = +2 and
{{w7_neutral_med_am2}} at α = −2 — and the above-τ rate by {{w7_neutral_dpm_abs}}. **A direction
that acts on estimated magnitude behaves exactly as observed.**

### 6.5 The verbalized belief does not move either

| arm, L{{layer_primary}}, above-favoured | correct / incorrect / unclear | labelled n | P(believes above) |
|---|---|---|---|
| α = +2 | {{w7_v_ap2}} | {{w7_nlab_ap2}} | {{w7_phat_ap2}} |
| **sham** | {{w7_v_sham}} | {{w7_nlab_sham}} | **{{w7_phat_sham}}** |
| α = −2 | {{w7_v_am2}} | {{w7_nlab_am2}} | {{w7_phat_am2}} |

The pre-registered flip is {{w7_flip}}, interval [{{w7_flip_lo}}, {{w7_flip_hi}}]. **The sign is
the predicted one — the only pre-registered statistic in the project that gets its predicted sign
— and the interval includes zero, so the flip is not established.** Three things cut against it
even at face value. It is **one-sided against the sham**: the +2 arm moves
{{w7_flip_plus_vs_sham}} and the −2 arm {{w7_flip_minus_vs_sham}}, so the entire contrast is the
negative arm suppressing belief-in-above. **A random direction moved it more**: a screen frozen in
the pre-registration forced two of the {{n_null_directions}} random arms to be judged, and one
reaches P(believes above) = {{w7_null04_phat}} against v_p̂'s {{w7_phat_ap2}} and the sham's
{{w7_phat_sham}} — *a screen-selected and therefore biased pair, so a caution rather than a test*.
And **the mirrored arm kills it**: on the below-favoured condition the same ±2 injection gives
{{w7_below_phat_ap2}} and {{w7_below_phat_am2}}, no movement at all, where a direction that
causally sets the believed side should move both arms. The no-bet arms are a clean judge control —
mention rate {{w7_neutral_mention}} and every verdict *unclear*.

### 6.6 The low-dose follow-up, and a gate that fired on its own noise

**Status label, carried by every number in this subsection.** The follow-up was **designed after
the main result was known** — the doses were chosen *because* the pre-registered doses failed. Its
rules were frozen before its data, which is what that buys and nothing more, and **it does not
reopen the main verdict.**

**Coherence and content markers agree that these doses do not distort.** Coherence is
{{w7b_coh}} in all {{n_w7b_arms}} arms; {{w7b_trunc}} truncated and {{w7b_degen}} degenerate in
{{n_w7b_gens}}; output lengths {{w7b_tok_min}}–{{w7b_tok_max}} against the unsteered
{{w3_B_above_tokens}}; median log₁₀ estimates {{w7b_medlog_min}}–{{w7b_medlog_max}} against the
unsteered {{w3_unsteered_medlog}}. Engagement with the bet is *higher* than at the main packet's
doses, {{sk_w7b_mention_mean}} against the sham's {{sk_w7_sham_mention}}.

**Result.** Δ±(v_p̂) at ±0.5 is **{{w7b_dpm}}**, interval [{{w7b_dpm_lo}}, {{w7b_dpm_hi}}] (judge
{{w7b_dpm_j}}, [{{w7b_dpm_j_lo}}, {{w7b_dpm_j_hi}}]). The sign is, for the first time, the
pre-registered one. It is not distinguishable from zero, it **reverses** at half that dose
({{w7b_dpm_quarter}}), and the four random directions do the same contrast at mean
{{w7b_null_mean}} — one reaching {{w7b_null_max}} on an interval that excludes zero where v_p̂'s
does not.

**The frozen distortion gate fired, and it should not be trusted.** The gate averages, over the
eight random arms, the absolute difference between each arm's landing rate and the sham's, and
declares distortion above {{lf_dbar_line}}. Observed: {{w7b_dbar}} on the corrected basis and
{{w7b_dbar_j}} on the judge basis, so the "even this dose distorts" row fired and **stands as the
verdict of record**. But that statistic is a mean of absolute differences between binomial
proportions at n = {{conv_n_per_arm}} and has a non-zero floor. Computed exactly under the null
the gate exists to detect — every arm the same coin, the injection doing nothing —
**E[D̄] = {{sk_dbar_E}} and P(D̄ > {{lf_dbar_line}}) = {{sk_dbar_P}}**. **A design that does nothing
whatsoever trips this gate about two thirds of the time**, so the two rows that would have
licensed a statement *about the direction* were jointly unreachable before a single token was
generated. The verdict row is reported, and reported as weakly informative by construction.

**What the arms actually look like: one common rate.** The {{n_w7b_arms}} arms are mutually
homogeneous — χ² = {{sk_chi2}} on {{sk_dof}} degrees of freedom, p = {{sk_chi2_p}} — consistent
with a single landing rate across the value direction *and* random directions, both signs and both
dose sizes. Pooled: {{sk_pooled_k}}/{{sk_pooled_n}} = {{sk_pooled_rate}}. That rate sits below the
α = 0 references (Fisher p = {{sk_fisher_sham}} against the sham) **but does not scale with
dose**: {{sk_quarter_rate}} at the smaller dose against {{sk_half_rate}} at twice the dose, Fisher
p = {{sk_dose_p}}, a difference of {{sk_dose_delta}}. **A distortion flat in dose is not a
distortion story.** The most economical reading at |α| ≤ 1 is one common rate near half with
sampling scatter, and an α = 0 reference at n = {{conv_n_per_arm}} reading high — and **the packet
cannot separate those, because it reused the earlier sham rather than generating a fresh one**, a
limitation declared before the data. *The homogeneity analysis is descriptive; no verdict rests on
it.*

### 6.7 What the causal work does establish

**Injecting along v_p̂ is powerfully causal on the estimate and is not believed-side-specific
[measured].** The most economical description of v_p̂ is a direction with a large component along
**estimated numeric magnitude**, whose believed-side content — real enough to decode at
{{w5_B_balacc_lstar}} — is not what dominates when it is written back in. The evidence is §6.4's
three control arms together: the effect survives deleting the bet, does not mirror, and is matched
in size by random directions (mean Δ_j = {{w7_null_mean}}).

**A bound [measured].** Whatever v_p̂-specific landing effect exists at
{{d_a025_pct}}–{{d_a05_pct}} % of the residual norm is smaller than four random directions'
typical excursion at the same norm, at {{conv_n_per_arm}} generations per arm.

**And the design's own limit.** The pre-registered grid may sit entirely in a regime where generic
distortion dominates. Its smallest dose, {{d_a1_pct}} % of the residual norm, is already
**symmetric** in α (Δ+ = {{w7_dplus_a1}}, Δ− = {{w7_dminus_a1}}) — what a pure magnitude effect
looks like, not what a believed-side effect looks like — and the follow-up went lower and found a
flat offset rather than a gradient. **No direction-specific effect, and a direction-specific
effect below this design's resolving power, are not separated by anything in this project.**

